## 3. Target Audience & Searcher Profile

The searcher is a prospective renter, most likely arriving from out of state or moving from Manhattan, who has decided Brooklyn is the right borough and now needs to understand how the neighborhoods differ from a practical standpoint. They are in the **comparison stage**: they have a budget in mind, a general lifestyle preference, and a commute constraint, but they do not yet know which neighborhood names match those criteria. They expect a concise but specific guide that gives them enough information to narrow a shortlist and take their next step, without requiring them to read a 5,000-word encyclopedia. They are not looking for a list of every neighborhood in Brooklyn; they want a functional map of the major options organized by what matters to a renter.

